# Domain Data

## ErrorCatalog (`lib/ErrorCatalog.json`)

Keys match IIB failure identifiers (e.g. `Environment - failure`, `Clock accuracy - failure`).

Each entry:

```json
{
  "title": "Short title",
  "userMessage": "Plain-language explanation for students",
  "causes": ["..."],
  "fixes": ["Run: .\\prepare.ps1 -Apply", "..."]
}
```

- `userMessage` and `fixes` must be student-friendly (no jargon)
- `fixes` may reference toolkit commands (`.\prepare.ps1 -Apply`, `.\inspera-preflight.ps1`)

## Blocklist (`data/default-blocklist.json`)

- `processes[]`: `{ "name": "Discord.exe", "category": "remote-access|recording|chat|vm|..." }`
- `processNamePatterns[]`: regex patterns with categories
- Runtime also merges names extracted from IIB logs

## Config (`data/config.json`)

- `logDirectories`: search paths in order; supports `%USERNAME%`, `%USERPROFILE%`, `%TEMP%`
- `fallbackToUserTemp`: also search current user's `%TEMP%`
- `insperaUrl`: default for network checks; log tenant overrides when available

Shipped in `dist/InsperaExamHelper/data/` — edit source, then rebuild.
